# L §5.14.1, §8.3 (tally 2.1.7, S9's family; the review's non-blocking item 5, pick P41): a def that holds bal(x) with
# no day and that no decision reaches is LOAD-READS at load, whatever the asks, and like every load refusal it names
# the read's file and line. refcore 2.1.7 printed it with neither.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
input y: int

def nd: money PLN = bal(konto)

ask r: y

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  y = 1
=== expect
refused: LOAD-READS nd holds bal(x) with no day: a running read outside a decision and its defs (m.tally:12)
